<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Key points</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list {"className":"ifm-ticks"} -->
<ul class="wp-block-list ifm-ticks"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Post regularly and usefully, and do not chase viral hits.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Mix four kinds of post: helpful, proof, personal and offers.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Three posts a week is enough for most small businesses.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Real photos from your phone do better than stock images.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The hardest part of social media for a small business is not the posting. It is knowing what to post. This list gives you twenty ideas that work for almost any trade, grouped into four types, plus a simple weekly routine for using them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Helpful posts</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These answer the questions customers ask you every week. They show you know your trade and they are the posts people save and share.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>1. A quick tip related to your trade.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>2. The answer to a question you were asked this week.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>3. A common mistake and how to avoid it.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>4. A seasonal reminder: boilers in autumn, gardens in spring.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>5. What something typically costs and what changes the price.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Proof posts</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>People trust what they can see. Proof posts show the work and the customers behind it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>6. A before and after photo.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>7. A finished job, with a line about what was involved.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>8. A customer review, with their permission.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>9. A short video of a job in progress.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>10. A problem you were called in to fix.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Personal posts</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Small businesses have an advantage over big ones: real people. Use it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>11. Who you are and why you started.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>12. Meet a member of the team.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>13. A look behind the scenes: the van, the workshop, the kitchen.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>14. A local event, charity or supplier you support.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>15. A milestone, such as an anniversary or a new piece of kit.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Offer posts</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Keep these to about one post in five. A feed that only sells gets ignored.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>16. A limited-time offer with a clear end date.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>17. A new service or product.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>18. Availability: "two slots left this month".</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>19. A reminder of something people forget you do.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>20. A simple call to action: how to book, call or order.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

